    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "01\nMake the caller supply the limits\nLocal defaults + per-consumer knobs\n→\nRequired policy inputs\nOutput capture, spooling, framing, resources, lifecycle and diagnostics read the e",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-required",
        "data-decision": "required"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "02\nKeep the operating envelope\nExisting values, formulas and untimed waits\n→\nSame values, one policy definition\nDefaults are retained. Memory limits still depend on host memory. No",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-values",
        "data-decision": "values"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "03\nLet composition choose the response clock\nStatus action supplies 100 ms directly\n→\nStatus-observer purpose selects 100 ms\nThe purpose belongs to a transport instance, not to a m",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-purpose",
        "data-decision": "purpose"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "04\nCount attempts in their own scopes\nOne-shot reattach / resume / startup retry\n→\nThree numeric limits, all default to 1\nReattachment spans accepted execution; fetch-resume state ",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-budgets",
        "data-decision": "budgets"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "05\nExpose the reattached completion's error\nRecovery failure rethrows first accepted-close error\n→\nLater completion can expose its own error\nAfter an accepted close, a corrupt comp",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-error",
        "data-decision": "error"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "06\nUse different input shapes at different depths\nDefaults hidden in consumers and helpers\n→\nSnapshot → sections → fields → numbers\nSome consumers take several sections, others one",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-shapes",
        "data-decision": "shapes"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "07\nKeep old tuning calls in test adapters\nTests tune production constructors\n→\nSeven helper files translate into policies\nTest-only wrappers preserve legacy calls and construct val",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-adapters",
        "data-decision": "adapters"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "08\nMake wrappers look like the former APIs\nProduction classes at test import sites\n→\nAdapters aliased to production class names\nTests often keep names such as LocalDaemonTransport ",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-aliases",
        "data-decision": "aliases"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "09\nLet adapters rewrite the requested test limits\nInline 0 means spill immediately\n→\nClient inline floor becomes 64 KiB\nThe client helper also creates the output directory. The dae",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-rewrite",
        "data-decision": "rewrite"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "10\nReshape test payloads around valid policy limits\nTiny or zero standalone limits\n→\nCoordinated chunk / inline / result values\ncapture(1) becomes capture(32); one two-byte record ",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-fixtures",
        "data-decision": "fixtures"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "11\nMove the resource-policy test surface\nCLI memory recipe + three test definitions\n→\nExisting package policy tests + consumer tests\nThe duplicate CLI recipe and its derivation/con",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-tests",
        "data-decision": "tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "12\nDelete a startup deadline input that was unused\nstartupTimeoutMs stored but never read\n→\nField and test arguments removed\nRemoving this input does not remove an active startup t",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-dead",
        "data-decision": "dead"
      }
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "13\nGuard the retired names in production source\nMeta-test checks three policy bypass strings\n→\nMeta-test checks 36 retired strings\nThe guard scans CLI production source and exclude",
      "attrs": {
        "href": "#decision-fence",
        "data-decision": "fence"
      }
    },
